  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b3b563d715eb6c64c9b6c779e47f3352, type: 3}
  m_Name: Day4Letter
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Category: 2
  Prefab: {fileID: 6625514644646704096, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  Interactable: {fileID: 5048261325816738630, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  TextFields:
  - 
  - "Astrid\u2014\n\nSo\u2014you really left Martha\u2019s. I\u2019m proud of you.
    It\u2019s time. If things slow down here, I\u2019d love to come visit. The observatory
    sounds cool. All the painting? Classic Elijah. \r\n\nThanks for telling me about
    your idea for the story. Most people don\u2019t even know the CERES network still
    works\u2014let alone that you and Elijah might be close to unlocking one of the
    satellites. And if he\u2019s right, that there\u2019s something buried in the
    old data people need to see\u2026 yeah. That needs to get out.\r\n\nYou should
    write to Nadine Cho. She's running Features now. I mentioned you\u2014just enough
    to spark interest. She's thoughtful, and she\u2019s looking for stories with
    real urgency. If you\u2019re ready, send her a pitch.\r\n\nWe\u2019re still getting
    a weekly edition out across the Midwest. Nothing digital obviously\u2014just
    print. It\u2019s all manual: layout by hand, old press running in Bronzeville.
    Barely hanging on, but it works. I love the feeling of the old tools. \r\n\nCan\u2019t
    believe you missed Elijah by just a few days. Heartbreaker. At least he's sending
    you messages. I still don\u2019t get why they won\u2019t ease up on the broadcast
    restrictions. Half the bands are jammed, and the rest are so heavily monitored
    no one wants to risk using them. You\u2019d think with everything at stake, they\u2019d
    want people like you getting through. It must be driving you crazy to have to
    only hear from him every few weeks over post. \r\n\nWrite soon\u2014let me know
    how the project is coming. \r\nYour ink-and-paper penpal, \n   \u2014Marisol"
  - "P.S. If you ever get satellite access, please promise the first thing you\u2019ll
    broadcast is a mixtape."
  StreamingVisuals: []
  DefaultPinnedPos: {x: 0.91, y: 1.79, z: 0.01}
